  "reviewed_invariants": [
    "Ordered stop/restart/seek increments checked u64 identity only in staged final audio declarations; overflow and invalid scalar/role preserve prior world and queue.",
    "Unchanged SetPlaying preserves old pause/resume behavior; explicit transport epoch forces existing bounded retirement/replacement path without cursor approximation or unacknowledged voice overlap.",
    "Scene v19 appends epochs only for nonzero transport sources; old writers retain prior versions/bytes. Reader bounds and mandatory capability predicates remain checked.",
    "Audio checkpoint v2 uses bounded 33-byte source rows and validates consumed epoch against the exact world before restoring mixer; all-zero owners retain v1 encoding.",
    "Primitive TS args and existing caught-command poisoning preserve whole-tick rejection. No authoring or backend action from command parser.",
    "Actual source tests cover repeated ended static/stream replay, stopped seek, ordered controls, epoch precision/exhaustion, consumed-world mismatch and PCM continuation."
  ],
